# TCC Billing System

A web-based billing and payment portal for **Torres Capitol College**. Students can see an itemized assessment of fees, submit payments and download official receipts. Cashiers verify and record payments. Administrators manage accounts, fees and semesters.

It works in any browser, can be installed on a phone as an app (PWA), and also runs inside an Android WebView app.

> Capstone project, BSIT. Built by Paul Harvey C. Ampoyo.

---

## Features

**Students**
- Create an account (with password confirmation); the Business Office approves it before first sign-in
- Sign in with Student ID or email; reset a forgotten password by email
- Itemized **Assessment of Fees** with total charges, payments, discounts and remaining balance
- Submit GCash, bank or over-the-counter payments with a reference number
- Payment history, **official receipts (PDF)** and a printable statement of account

**Cashiers**
- Cashier terminal to find a student and collect a payment
- Verify or reject payments submitted by students
- Student accounts, transaction list with filters and **CSV export**
- Approve or reject new registrations

**Administrators**
- Overview dashboard with collection statistics
- Create cashier and admin accounts (only admins can do this), reset passwords, deactivate accounts
- Billing setup: fee types, academic semesters with exam dates, bulk billing
- Apply discounts, cancel bills, void payments (every correction is recorded)
- Audit log of important actions and an email test tool

**General**
- Light and dark mode, responsive layout, installable as an app
- Receipts show the cashier's name and employee ID; statements show who assessed the bill

## Fee schedule

Every new student receives the same line items. Only the year-level total changes, and it drops by ₱2,000 each year.

| Year level | Total assessment |
|---|---|
| 1st year | ₱20,000.00 |
| 2nd year | ₱18,000.00 |
| 3rd year | ₱16,000.00 |
| 4th year | ₱14,000.00 |

Flat fees (₱2,980.00 for everyone): Registration, Tinagong Kinaadman, Cyber Views, Teacher's Subsidy, School System, PRISAA, GPTCA. The remainder is split 60% Tuition, 15% Misc. Fees, 18% Computer Laboratory and 7% Internet. To change the numbers, edit `YEAR_TOTALS`, `FLAT` and `SHARE` near the top of `server.js`.

## Tech stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | HTML, CSS, vanilla JavaScript (PWA with service worker) |
| Backend | Node.js 22, Express 5 |
| Database | PostgreSQL on Supabase |
| Auth | JSON Web Tokens, bcrypt password hashing |
| Email | Nodemailer with Gmail |
| Hosting | Vercel |
| Mobile | Android WebView app (separate `android-app` project) |

## Project structure

```
├── server.js              Express API and business rules
├── vercel.json            Vercel build and routing settings
├── package.json
├── .env.example           Template for environment variables
├── database/              SQL scripts for Supabase
└── public/                Website files served to the browser
    ├── index.html
    ├── app.js
    ├── style.css
    ├── sw.js              Service worker (offline shell)
    ├── manifest.json      App install settings
    └── logo.png, icon-192.png, icon-512.png
```

## Environment variables

| Name | Required | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `DATABASE_URL` | Yes | Supabase **Transaction pooler** connection string (port 6543) |
| `JWT_SECRET` | Yes | Long random string used to sign login tokens |
| `EMAIL_USER` | For email | Gmail address that sends receipts and reset links |
| `EMAIL_PASS` | For email | Gmail **App Password** (16 characters, no spaces) |
| `APP_URL` | Recommended | Public site address, used in password-reset links |
| `EMAIL_SERVICE` | No | Defaults to `gmail` |

Without `EMAIL_USER` and `EMAIL_PASS` the system still works. Receipts are simply not emailed and password reset by email is unavailable.

## Run locally

```bash
npm install
cp .env.example .env      # then fill in the real values
npm run dev               # http://localhost:3000
```

## Set up the database

In Supabase, open **SQL Editor** and run the scripts in `database/` in order:

1. `01-payments-and-fee-types.sql`
2. `02-itemized-assessment.sql`

Make sure the `fee_types` table has at least one row (for example "Tuition").

**Create the first admin:** register a normal account on the website, then run:

```sql
UPDATE users SET role = 'admin', status = 'approved' WHERE email = 'you@example.com';
```

From then on the admin creates cashier accounts under **Users & staff**. `database/cleanup-test-accounts.sql` removes every non-admin account and is meant for clearing test data before a demo.

## Deploy to Vercel

1. Push this project to GitHub.
2. In Vercel, import the repository (Framework Preset: **Other**).
3. Add the environment variables above under **Settings → Environment Variables** (Production).
4. Deploy. After changing a variable, **redeploy**, because variables apply only to new deployments.

## Email setup (Gmail)

1. Turn on **2-Step Verification** in the Google account.
2. Open <https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords>, create an app password and copy the 16 characters.
3. Set `EMAIL_USER` to the Gmail address and `EMAIL_PASS` to the app password (no spaces).
4. Redeploy, then sign in as admin and use **Users & staff → Send test email**. If it fails, the exact reason is shown.

## Security notes

- Passwords are hashed with bcrypt; sessions use signed tokens that expire after 12 hours
- Role checks are enforced on the server for every protected route
- Sign-in and password-reset attempts are rate limited
- All database queries are parameterized
- Students can only open their own statements and receipts
- Secrets live in environment variables and are never committed

## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Fix |
|---|---|
| Build fails on Vercel | Check that `vercel.json` points to `server.js` and that `public/` exists |
| Database connection errors | Use the **Transaction pooler** string; encode special characters in the password |
| "self-signed certificate" | Remove `?sslmode=...` from the end of `DATABASE_URL` |
| Emails do not arrive | Use **Send test email**; check the App Password, spam folder and Vercel logs |
| Cannot sign in after registering | An admin or cashier must approve the registration first |